Models and tools Infinity can download or run
---------------------------------------------
Infinity does not include any model weights. When you choose one in Models by job,
it is downloaded from its publisher and is covered by that publisher's licence:

- FLUX.2 [klein] 4B, Black Forest Labs (Apache License 2.0)
- Z-Image Turbo, Tongyi-MAI / Alibaba (Apache License 2.0)
- EmbeddingGemma, Google (Gemma Terms of Use, https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms)
- Whisper models via whisper.cpp (MIT License)
- Models run through Ollama, LM Studio, MLX LM, vLLM, llama.cpp or Jan, and models found in
  Find models on Hugging Face, under each model's own licence (shown as a badge in Find models).
  Some of the ones Infinity suggests:
  - Llama 3.x, Meta (Llama Community License; "Built with Llama")
  - Gemma 3, Google (Gemma Terms of Use)
  - Qwen 2.5 and Qwen 3, Alibaba (Apache License 2.0, some sizes under the Qwen License)
  - Mistral 7B, Mistral AI (Apache License 2.0)
  - DeepSeek R1, DeepSeek (MIT License)
  - gpt-oss, OpenAI (Apache License 2.0)

Local engines Infinity can install or start on request, each under its own licence:
Ollama (MIT), MLX and MLX LM (MIT), vLLM (Apache License 2.0), llama.cpp (MIT).

Local image models run through mflux (MIT License, https://github.com/filipstrand/mflux),
which Infinity installs with uv on request.

Infinity Assistant ports ideas from OpenMausBot (Apache License 2.0,
https://github.com/milind-soni/OpenMausBot).
